{"4944320": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Twin Drive", "steam_appid": 4944320, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Twin Drive splits a single car in half. Literally. Player 1 drives the front axle, Player 2 drives the rear, each with their own engine, gearbox, and steering. Push forward in sync and the car takes off. Fight the wheel against each other while both flooring it, and it breaks loose into a smoking, screeching donut.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>One Car, Two Drivers</strong> There's no shared control scheme here. Each player genuinely owns half the car's physics. Steering, acceleration, and braking are split down the middle, so getting anywhere in a straight line takes real coordination, not just two people mashing the same controls.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Deliver Under Pressure</strong> Pick up orders and race them across the map before the timer runs out. Deliveries get harder and pay more the farther you have to go, and missing the deadline means the order is gone.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>When It Goes Wrong (And It Will)</strong> Hard crashes send your drivers physically flying. Full ragdoll physics react to every impact, mid drive. Half the fun is watching your co-driver get thrown around when a delivery goes sideways.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Hang Out Before You Drive</strong> Before each match, both players spawn into a low stakes junkyard to goof around in their own half cars, talk over voice chat, and warm up before the real driving starts.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Play With a Friend, Anywhere</strong> No split screen, no shared keyboard. Play online with a friend, each from your own machine, with your own camera and your own seat in the same car, and full voice chat.</p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Twin Drive splits a single car in half. Literally. Player 1 drives the front axle, Player 2 drives the rear, each with their own engine, gearbox, and steering. Push forward in sync and the car takes off. Fight the wheel against each other while both flooring it, and it breaks loose into a smoking, screeching donut.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>One Car, Two Drivers</strong> There's no shared control scheme here. Each player genuinely owns half the car's physics. Steering, acceleration, and braking are split down the middle, so getting anywhere in a straight line takes real coordination, not just two people mashing the same controls.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Deliver Under Pressure</strong> Pick up orders and race them across the map before the timer runs out. Deliveries get harder and pay more the farther you have to go, and missing the deadline means the order is gone.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>When It Goes Wrong (And It Will)</strong> Hard crashes send your drivers physically flying. Full ragdoll physics react to every impact, mid drive. Half the fun is watching your co-driver get thrown around when a delivery goes sideways.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Hang Out Before You Drive</strong> Before each match, both players spawn into a low stakes junkyard to goof around in their own half cars, talk over voice chat, and warm up before the real driving starts.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Play With a Friend, Anywhere</strong> No split screen, no shared keyboard. Play online with a friend, each from your own machine, with your own camera and your own seat in the same car, and full voice chat.</p>", "short_description": "Twin Drive is a 2 player online co-op driving game built around one gimmick: a single car split in half. One player drives the front, the other drives the rear. Stay in sync to steer straight, or fight each other into a screeching donut. Team up to deliver orders before the clock runs out.", "supported_languages": "English", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/